--TEST--
A `Core\Script\Handle` that a child task returns names no started script in the task that receives it, so `await` on it there throws and the task's own script at the same position is left alone — `rule:security/isolate-shares-nothing`
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.script]
spawn = true
--FILE own.nvs--
<?nvs
echo "from the own script";
--FILE task.nvs--
<?nvs
echo "from the task's script";
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:concurrency/isolates-spawn-script-and-await
// A task returns a script handle, and `await` on it outside the task throws an error.
// The program's own script is still waiting for its own `await`.

var $own = spawn script "own.nvs" with(output: "capture");
var $result = Core\Task::all({
    job: fn (): Core\Script\Handle => spawn script "task.nvs" with(output: "capture"),
});
echo "the task returned its handle\n";
try {
    var $taken = await $result->job;
    echo "this line does not run\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "used outside the task: ", $e->message, "\n";
}
var $done = await $own;
echo "own output: ", $done->output, "\n";
--EXPECT--
the task returned its handle
used outside the task: `await` was given a handle a previous `await` already collected
own output: from the own script
